#: ../../usage.md:1
msgid "Usage"
msgstr "Utilisation"

#: ../../usage.md:3
msgid "Standard `django.tasks` API — no custom decorator:"
msgstr "API standard de `django.tasks` — sans décorateur propriétaire:"

#: ../../usage.md:15
msgid ""
"Per-task retry override: `@task(queue_name=\"emails\", max_attempts=1)`. "
"Overrides `OPTIONS[\"max_attempts\"]` for that task only; tasks that "
"don't set it keep using the backend-wide default."
msgstr ""
"Surcharge des réessais par tâche: `@task(queue_name=\"emails\", "
"max_attempts=1)`. Remplace `OPTIONS[\"max_attempts\"]` pour cette tâche "
"uniquement; les tâches qui ne le définissent pas continuent d'utiliser la "
"valeur par défaut du backend."

#: ../../usage.md:17
msgid ""
"Coroutines (`async def`) work out of the box — `Task.call()` bridges them"
" via `async_to_sync` internally, no asyncio event loop needed in the "
"worker."
msgstr ""
"Les coroutines (`async def`) fonctionnent sans configuration "
"supplémentaire — `Task.call()` les relie via `async_to_sync` en interne, "
"aucune boucle d'événements asyncio n'est nécessaire dans le worker."

#: ../../usage.md:19
msgid "Running the worker"
msgstr "Exécuter le worker"

#: ../../usage.md:25
msgid "`--batch`: drain the queue then exit (useful for a Kubernetes Job)."
msgstr ""
"`--batch`: vide la file puis quitte (utile pour un Job Kubernetes)."

#: ../../usage.md:26
msgid "`--max-tasks N`: exit after roughly N tasks."
msgstr "`--max-tasks N`: quitte après environ N tâches."

#: ../../usage.md:27
msgid "`--backend default`: which `TASKS` alias to process."
msgstr "`--backend default`: quel alias `TASKS` traiter."

#: ../../usage.md:29
msgid "Django admin"
msgstr "Admin Django"

#: ../../usage.md:31
msgid "`TaskRow` is registered read-only in the Django admin for inspection."
msgstr ""
"`TaskRow` est enregistré en lecture seule dans l'admin Django à des fins "
"d'inspection."

#: ../../usage.md:33
msgid "OpenTelemetry (optional)"
msgstr "OpenTelemetry (optionnel)"

#: ../../usage.md:39
msgid ""
"Installing the `otel` extra (`opentelemetry-api` only) wraps every task "
"execution in a span named `<TASK_WORKER_SPAN_PREFIX>.<task_path>` "
"(attributes: `django_task_psql.attempt`, `django_task_psql.queue_name`), "
"with exceptions recorded and the span marked as an error. Nothing is "
"exported unless your app configures a `TracerProvider` and exporter "
"itself (e.g. `opentelemetry-sdk` + an OTLP exporter); without "
"`opentelemetry-api` installed at all, tracing is skipped entirely with "
"zero import errors."
msgstr ""
"L'installation de l'extra `otel` (`opentelemetry-api` seulement) enveloppe "
"chaque exécution de tâche dans un span nommé "
"`<TASK_WORKER_SPAN_PREFIX>.<task_path>` (attributs: "
"`django_task_psql.attempt`, `django_task_psql.queue_name`), avec les "
"exceptions enregistrées et le span marqué comme erreur. Rien n'est "
"exporté sauf si votre application configure elle-même un "
"`TracerProvider` et un exporteur (par exemple `opentelemetry-sdk` + un "
"exporteur OTLP); sans `opentelemetry-api` installé du tout, le traçage "
"est entièrement ignoré sans aucune erreur d'import."
